1
00:00:17,231 --> 00:00:21,610
Captioning made possible
by Lions Gate Entertainment

2
00:00:34,498 --> 00:00:35,624
<i>Game over.</i>

3
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:38,252
<i>I'll fuckin' kill you!</i>

4
00:00:38,294 --> 00:00:40,504
<i>You fuckin' bitch!</i>

5
00:00:41,672 --> 00:00:43,841
<i>Fuckin' bitch!</i>

6
00:00:44,925 --> 00:00:46,761
<i>I'll fucking kill you!</i>

7
00:00:47,803 --> 00:00:49,221
<i>Aagh!</i>

8
00:00:49,513 --> 00:00:51,098
<i>Aagh!</i>

9
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:17,685
<i>Daniel!</i>

10
00:05:12,317 --> 00:05:13,485
Clear the flank!

11
00:05:13,527 --> 00:05:14,278
<i>Left side clear!</i>

12
00:05:14,945 --> 00:05:15,738
Same here!

13
00:05:15,779 --> 00:05:16,989
We're clear!

14
00:05:17,031 --> 00:05:18,032
<i>Left side clear!</i>

15
00:05:18,115 --> 00:05:19,033
<i>We're clear!</i>

16
00:05:20,617 --> 00:05:21,744
<i>Back's clear.</i>

17
00:05:32,337 --> 00:05:33,964
Oh, my god.

18
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:37,676
Someone call Kerry.

19
00:05:39,344 --> 00:05:40,804
Call came in at 11:45.

20
00:05:40,846 --> 00:05:43,265
The woman heard an explosion.
Fire department was first on the scene.

21
00:05:43,348 --> 00:05:44,224
Kerry!

22
00:05:44,433 --> 00:05:45,976
-Is it him?
-Before you go in there.

23
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,604
Eric--is it him?

24
00:05:49,188 --> 00:05:50,481
They don't know yet.

25
00:05:59,031 --> 00:06:00,491
It's not detective Matthews.

26
00:06:14,046 --> 00:06:15,172
What happened?

27
00:06:15,422 --> 00:06:18,759
The victim was held
in place by these chains.

28
00:06:23,889 --> 00:06:25,182
Huh?

29
00:06:51,792 --> 00:06:53,418
Hello, Troy.

30
00:06:54,378 --> 00:06:56,338
I want to play a game.

31
00:06:57,005 --> 00:07:00,592
<i>This game will take place in a room</i>
<i>not much bigger than the room</i>

32
00:07:00,676 --> 00:07:04,221
you've spent most of your life in--
a prison cell.

33
00:07:05,139 --> 00:07:07,683
<i>Despite all of</i>
<i>the advantages and privileges</i>

34
00:07:07,724 --> 00:07:09,226
<i>that you were given at birth,</i>

35
00:07:09,268 --> 00:07:12,312
<i>you have returned to</i>
<i>prison again and again--</i>

36
00:07:12,938 --> 00:07:15,941
more comfortable in chains
then you are in freedom.

37
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:19,444
<i>Tonight, we will see how far</i>
<i>you are willing to go</i>

38
00:07:19,486 --> 00:07:22,406
to break those chains once and for all.

39
00:07:22,447 --> 00:07:26,577
Live or die, Troy. Make your choice.

40
00:07:45,179 --> 00:07:46,763
This was the bomb.

41
00:07:47,014 --> 00:07:49,016
All he had to do...

42
00:07:49,016 --> 00:07:51,476
was release himself
from each of the chains.

43
00:07:52,978 --> 00:07:55,147
<i>Walk out the door...</i>

44
00:07:55,189 --> 00:07:57,107
<i>before it went off.</i>

45
00:07:59,026 --> 00:08:00,194
All he had to do?

46
00:08:42,236 --> 00:08:43,654
Oh, god!

47
00:09:07,552 --> 00:09:08,720
Oh, god!

48
00:09:09,096 --> 00:09:12,015
Aagh!

49
00:09:35,289 --> 00:09:38,625
<i>What I don't understand is</i>
<i>how the hell could Jigsaw do all this?</i>

50
00:09:38,667 --> 00:09:41,753
He was damn near on his deathbed
the last time we saw him.

51
00:09:44,631 --> 00:09:48,260
I'm not so sure he did.
So far, this isn't following his patterns.

52
00:09:48,302 --> 00:09:49,177
Meaning?

53
00:09:49,261 --> 00:09:50,220
Well...

54
00:09:51,346 --> 00:09:52,556
how'd you get in here?

55
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:54,224
We cut the door down.

56
00:09:54,266 --> 00:09:55,142
<i> Why?</i>

57
00:09:55,183 --> 00:09:57,894
Because somebody heard an explosion
and called us.

58
00:09:57,936 --> 00:10:00,272
I mean, why did you have to
cut the door down?

59
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:03,734
It was welded shut.
A bloody truck couldn't get in here.

60
00:10:03,942 --> 00:10:05,110
Exactly.

61
00:10:05,152 --> 00:10:06,153
I don't follow.

62
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:09,281
If the aim of Jigsaw's game
was to get out before the bomb went off,

63
00:10:09,323 --> 00:10:11,450
then why was the door welded shut?

64
00:10:11,533 --> 00:10:13,577
<i>And the guy couldn't</i>
<i>get out if he wanted to.</i>

65
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:14,786
<i> You won't believe this.</i>

66
00:10:14,828 --> 00:10:16,663
We got the tape out clean.

67
00:11:12,135 --> 00:11:13,512
<i>Hello, Troy.</i>

68
00:11:13,553 --> 00:11:15,138
I want to play a game.

69
00:11:17,599 --> 00:11:21,269
Live or die, Troy. Make your choice.

70
00:13:20,388 --> 00:13:21,306
Hello, Kerry.

71
00:13:22,724 --> 00:13:24,351
I want to play a game.

72
00:13:25,185 --> 00:13:28,522
Up until now, you have spent you life
among the dead

73
00:13:28,563 --> 00:13:30,732
piecing together their final moments.

74
00:13:30,815 --> 00:13:33,693
<i>You're good at this</i>
<i>because you, like them,</i>

75
00:13:33,735 --> 00:13:35,237
<i>are also dead--</i>

76
00:13:35,487 --> 00:13:37,948
dead on the inside.

77
00:13:38,323 --> 00:13:43,995
You identify more with a cold corpse
than you do with a living human.

78
00:13:44,371 --> 00:13:47,582
I believe you want
to join your true family--

79
00:13:47,666 --> 00:13:49,876
indeed your only family--

80
00:13:49,918 --> 00:13:50,794
in death.

81
00:13:52,045 --> 00:13:55,966
The device you are wearing
is hooked into your ribcage.

82
00:13:56,007 --> 00:14:00,387
<i>And by the time this tape is finished,</i>
<i>you will have one minute</i>

83
00:14:00,428 --> 00:14:01,805
to find a way out.

84
00:14:01,846 --> 00:14:03,515
At the end of that minute...

85
00:14:04,307 --> 00:14:08,395
<i>you should know better than anyone</i>
<i>what happens then.</i>

86
00:14:08,645 --> 00:14:11,815
There is a single key
that will unlock the harness, Kerry.

87
00:14:11,898 --> 00:14:13,608
<i>It is right in front of you.</i>

88
00:14:13,692 --> 00:14:17,946
<i>All you have to do</i>
<i>is reach in and take it.</i>

89
00:14:18,613 --> 00:14:20,115
<i>But do it quickly.</i>

90
00:14:20,156 --> 00:14:22,659
The acid will dissolve the key

91
00:14:22,951 --> 00:14:24,995
<i>in a matter of seconds.</i>

92
00:14:25,453 --> 00:14:27,622
Make your choice.

93
00:15:45,659 --> 00:15:47,160
Come on.

94
00:15:48,161 --> 00:15:49,245
No!

95
00:16:01,758 --> 00:16:02,717
You.

96
00:16:38,712 --> 00:16:40,422
I gotta be at the hospital by 9:00.

97
00:16:43,258 --> 00:16:44,426
It's Tuesday.

98
00:16:44,467 --> 00:16:45,969
I thought you start at 11:00.

99
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:47,262
Yeah, well...

100
00:16:47,303 --> 00:16:49,264
they changed things on me last minute.

101
00:16:49,931 --> 00:16:51,266
<i>Well, you better head off then.</i>

102
00:16:58,565 --> 00:17:00,233
You're not gonna take a shower?

103
00:17:01,818 --> 00:17:02,736
Nah.

104
00:17:04,404 --> 00:17:06,197
I'm just gonna take
a shower at the hospital.

105
00:17:07,157 --> 00:17:08,533
Can we just...

106
00:17:09,242 --> 00:17:10,702
talk for 5 minutes?

107
00:17:11,661 --> 00:17:15,039
Hey, how about we just make eye contact
for 5 seconds.

108
00:17:15,081 --> 00:17:16,249
What's wrong?

109
00:17:17,125 --> 00:17:19,586
Nothing. It just...

110
00:17:20,211 --> 00:17:21,337
everything.

111
00:17:24,048 --> 00:17:24,966
<i>Lynn!</i>

112
00:17:25,008 --> 00:17:27,260
What is it you want from me, Chris?

113
00:17:29,304 --> 00:17:30,346
A divorce.

114
00:17:40,190 --> 00:17:41,274
50-A!

115
00:17:42,233 --> 00:17:45,361
Car skidded into on-coming traffic.
Pre-op 8!

116
00:17:45,403 --> 00:17:46,696
-Pressure?
-<i>80 over palp.</i>

117
00:17:46,738 --> 00:17:47,781
Pulse is ready.

118
00:17:48,323 --> 00:17:50,575
Ready? One, two, three.

119
00:17:50,617 --> 00:17:51,618
Where's Lynn?

120
00:17:51,618 --> 00:17:52,619
Page Dr. Denlon.

121
00:17:52,619 --> 00:17:53,620
Set up a heart line.

122
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:55,789
<i>Dr. Lynn Denlon,</i>
<i>please report to trauma immediately</i>

123
00:17:55,830 --> 00:17:59,167
<i>Dr. Lynn Denlon,</i>
<i>please report to trauma immediately.</i>

124
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:01,878
Lynn!

125
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,465
<i>Pressure's dropping rapidly.</i>

126
00:18:05,632 --> 00:18:06,716
<i>Pressure down to 70.</i>

127
00:18:06,758 --> 00:18:08,176
<i>He's going into shock.</i>

128
00:18:08,218 --> 00:18:09,636
<i>Get an O.R. Ready.</i>

129
00:18:09,844 --> 00:18:10,762
We've gotta crack his chest.

130
00:18:10,929 --> 00:18:12,722
<i>We've got a Volost 500 wide open.</i>

131
00:18:12,764 --> 00:18:13,807
No.

132
00:18:15,266 --> 00:18:16,142
What?

133
00:18:20,438 --> 00:18:21,898
No air entry on the right side.

134
00:18:21,981 --> 00:18:23,399
-<i>And?</i>
-It's not blood vessel tension.

135
00:18:23,483 --> 00:18:24,400
Let's get a chest tube in him.

136
00:18:24,442 --> 00:18:26,611
We gotta get him to O.R. Now.

137
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:28,279
<i>His stats are dropping.</i>

138
00:18:28,321 --> 00:18:29,739
<i>He's gonna code.</i>

139
00:18:31,699 --> 00:18:32,700
I'm doing it.

140
00:18:42,836 --> 00:18:43,878
I'm getting a rush of air.

141
00:18:44,963 --> 00:18:46,047
Stats are improving.

142
00:18:46,381 --> 00:18:47,882
Pressure back to 80.

143
00:18:48,675 --> 00:18:49,717
Pressure normal.

144
00:19:06,276 --> 00:19:08,152
Look, if you've got
something on your mind,

145
00:19:08,194 --> 00:19:09,070
go upstairs to psych.

146
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:12,198
Just don't bring it in here.
We don't have any seconds to spare, Lynn.

147
00:19:12,532 --> 00:19:15,451
The woman standing in front of me
had to be dragged from the locker room

148
00:19:15,493 --> 00:19:17,579
to put a chest tube in a trauma patient?

149
00:19:18,246 --> 00:19:20,039
Lynn Denlon should
have been the first one there.

150
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,086
Lynn!

151
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:26,880
<i>Lynn!</i>

152
00:20:01,331 --> 00:20:02,415
What the hell?

153
00:20:02,749 --> 00:20:04,250
I'm locked in.

154
00:20:04,292 --> 00:20:05,793
Is anybody there?

155
00:20:06,544 --> 00:20:07,587
Hello?

156
00:20:15,970 --> 00:20:17,221
Anybody here?

157
00:21:39,637 --> 00:21:41,014
What is this?!

158
00:21:41,097 --> 00:21:42,098
Help!

159
00:21:42,348 --> 00:21:44,183
Help me!

160
00:21:46,185 --> 00:21:47,145
Aagh!

161
00:21:47,186 --> 00:21:48,229
Help!

162
00:21:54,193 --> 00:21:55,194
<i>Who are you?</i>

163
00:21:55,236 --> 00:21:56,696
Who are you?!

164
00:21:56,988 --> 00:21:57,947
What is this?!

165
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:02,618
What are you doing?!

166
00:22:09,208 --> 00:22:10,752
Are you gonna behave?

167
00:22:18,468 --> 00:22:19,719
Let's go.

168
00:22:21,888 --> 00:22:23,097
What is this place?!

169
00:22:23,139 --> 00:22:24,766
What is this place?!

170
00:22:32,231 --> 00:22:35,985
What is-- what is--what...

171
00:22:43,117 --> 00:22:46,204
Who are you? Who are you?

172
00:22:46,245 --> 00:22:47,121
Aagh!

173
00:22:50,833 --> 00:22:52,460
Hello, Dr. Denlon.

174
00:22:52,668 --> 00:22:54,712
<i>You may not remember me,</i>

175
00:22:54,796 --> 00:22:57,006
but I most certainly remember you.

176
00:22:58,132 --> 00:22:59,509
I was a guest...

177
00:23:00,843 --> 00:23:02,804
at your hospital once.

178
00:23:06,432 --> 00:23:07,391
Where am I?

179
00:23:10,561 --> 00:23:12,480
Do you remember me?

180
00:23:22,198 --> 00:23:23,324
I've seen you on television.

181
00:23:25,243 --> 00:23:27,578
Lawrence Gordon was your Doctor.

182
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:29,413
I was his patent,

183
00:23:29,455 --> 00:23:30,915
and he was mine.

184
00:23:32,291 --> 00:23:36,129
As you can see from that report,
my prognosis isn't good.

185
00:23:38,131 --> 00:23:39,757
Would you agree?

186
00:23:46,305 --> 00:23:49,308
There's no preventative treatment
for what you have.

187
00:23:50,309 --> 00:23:53,229
I remember
you saying that to me once before

188
00:23:53,312 --> 00:23:55,231
in almost the exact same tone.

189
00:23:55,273 --> 00:23:58,943
Leave it to a Doctor
to find such a cold, clinical way

190
00:23:59,026 --> 00:24:01,070
of saying I'm a dead man walking.

191
00:24:02,196 --> 00:24:05,158
<i>Looking at me,</i>
<i>how long would you say I have left?</i>

192
00:24:05,616 --> 00:24:06,742
I'd have to examine you.

193
00:24:08,202 --> 00:24:10,204
Even then, a frontal lobe tumor

194
00:24:10,246 --> 00:24:11,289
<i>is unpredictable.</i>

195
00:24:11,330 --> 00:24:12,999
The growth depends on the rate of mitosis

196
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:13,791
versus apoptosis and--

197
00:24:13,833 --> 00:24:16,836
I'm sorry, but is all this

198
00:24:16,878 --> 00:24:19,005
<i>crude medical equipment around me</i>

199
00:24:19,046 --> 00:24:22,842
causing you to believe
that you're still inside a hospital?

200
00:24:23,634 --> 00:24:24,427
No.

201
00:24:24,468 --> 00:24:28,764
Then why are you speaking to me
in that graduate school medical jargon?

202
00:24:31,475 --> 00:24:32,685
Look at me!

203
00:24:32,727 --> 00:24:33,644
Aagh!

204
00:24:35,271 --> 00:24:36,564
Now you're looking.

205
00:24:36,939 --> 00:24:39,233
<i>I asked you a simple question.</i>

206
00:24:39,275 --> 00:24:41,277
<i>Based on your experience,</i>

207
00:24:41,319 --> 00:24:44,655
how long do you think I have left?

208
00:24:44,947 --> 00:24:46,866
It's not a simple answer.

209
00:24:46,908 --> 00:24:49,493
Based on your file, I'd say...

210
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:51,787
not long.

211
00:25:00,504 --> 00:25:03,174
<i>Death is a surprise party,</i>

212
00:25:03,216 --> 00:25:04,592
unless, of course...

213
00:25:05,593 --> 00:25:07,970
you're already dead on the inside.

214
00:25:11,974 --> 00:25:13,517
Unless you're the type of person

215
00:25:13,559 --> 00:25:14,727
who swallows...

216
00:25:14,769 --> 00:25:17,146
<i>antidepressants to hide the pain, eh,</i>

217
00:25:17,188 --> 00:25:19,899
turns their back on their husband,

218
00:25:19,941 --> 00:25:21,943
neglects their child.

219
00:25:21,984 --> 00:25:27,156
Who has every possible advantage in life
but then chooses not to advance.

220
00:25:27,198 --> 00:25:29,408
Oh, god.
What do you want from me?

221
00:25:30,785 --> 00:25:32,245
What do I want?

222
00:25:34,413 --> 00:25:35,957
I want to play a game.

223
00:25:39,210 --> 00:25:41,629
The rules of the game are simple...

224
00:25:42,713 --> 00:25:45,800
consequences of breaking them are great--

225
00:25:47,009 --> 00:25:47,885
death.

226
00:25:49,553 --> 00:25:52,848
<i>You're being tested.</i>
<i>Your will is being tested--</i>

227
00:25:52,890 --> 00:25:55,101
<i>your will to keep someone alive.</i>

228
00:25:55,226 --> 00:25:56,227
Can you do that?

229
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:57,812
<i>Can you follow the rules</i>

230
00:25:57,895 --> 00:25:59,605
and grant someone the gift of life?

231
00:25:59,647 --> 00:26:00,648
What--what is this?!

232
00:26:00,690 --> 00:26:02,608
No! Get it--aagh!

233
00:26:02,650 --> 00:26:04,485
No! No! No!

234
00:26:04,527 --> 00:26:05,361
What is this?!

235
00:26:05,403 --> 00:26:07,321
What are you doing to me?!

236
00:26:08,030 --> 00:26:09,740
Aagh!

237
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:17,832
The device that you're wearing
is linked to my heart-rate monitor.

238
00:26:17,915 --> 00:26:20,626
<i>The second</i>
<i>that heart-rate monitor flatlines,</i>

239
00:26:20,668 --> 00:26:25,464
or you move out of range,
an explosion will go off in that collar.

240
00:26:25,506 --> 00:26:28,342
<i>Your life and my life</i>

241
00:26:28,384 --> 00:26:30,011
<i>will end simultaneously.</i>

242
00:26:31,470 --> 00:26:32,179
Please.

243
00:26:32,221 --> 00:26:35,308
Please don't do this to me.
I have a family.

244
00:26:35,349 --> 00:26:36,267
<i>I have a family.</i>

245
00:26:36,517 --> 00:26:39,603
Let me give you the simple version.

246
00:26:40,354 --> 00:26:42,315
You will keep him alive--

247
00:26:42,356 --> 00:26:43,983
whatever it takes.

248
00:26:45,276 --> 00:26:48,571
<i>No excuses, no equivocations.</i>

249
00:26:48,904 --> 00:26:50,323
No crying.

250
00:26:50,364 --> 00:26:53,451
What do you mean, "keep him alive"?

251
00:26:55,828 --> 00:26:58,205
Out there on those screens

252
00:26:58,706 --> 00:27:01,167
<i>we have another test subject...</i>

253
00:27:01,167 --> 00:27:03,127
a man.

254
00:27:05,046 --> 00:27:06,172
He will face...

255
00:27:07,381 --> 00:27:08,674
A series of tests.

256
00:27:10,426 --> 00:27:11,969
<i>You have to keep John alive</i>

257
00:27:12,386 --> 00:27:15,014
until he makes it through.

258
00:27:15,056 --> 00:27:17,516
If he completes all of his tests

259
00:27:17,558 --> 00:27:19,894
and John is still breathing,

260
00:27:19,935 --> 00:27:22,855
then I will remove your collar

261
00:27:23,939 --> 00:27:25,399
and you're free to go.

262
00:27:27,151 --> 00:27:29,195
You're a vital piece
of my puzzle, Dr. Denlon--

263
