I've wanted to kill him every day...

785
01:21:37,648 --> 01:21:38,733
<i>Oh, my god!</i>

786
01:21:38,774 --> 01:21:39,609
...for 3 years.

787
01:21:39,650 --> 01:21:40,901
I wanted to kill you.

788
01:21:42,445 --> 01:21:43,404
<i> Jeff?</i>

789
01:21:43,446 --> 01:21:44,405
Maybe I am.

790
01:21:57,418 --> 01:21:58,419
<i> Ok.</i>

791
01:22:16,646 --> 01:22:17,647
Hold on, son.

792
01:22:19,273 --> 01:22:21,776
<i>God! God! God!</i>

793
01:22:55,476 --> 01:22:56,394
I got the key.

794
01:23:16,539 --> 01:23:20,334
<i>Help me! Help! Help me!</i>

795
01:23:27,216 --> 01:23:28,801
Help me!

796
01:23:30,136 --> 01:23:32,388
I can't stop it!

797
01:23:34,432 --> 01:23:36,392
I can't stop it!

798
01:23:44,150 --> 01:23:45,943
<i>God damn you!</i>

799
01:24:12,970 --> 01:24:14,930
<i>Don't you think it would be wise</i>

800
01:24:15,139 --> 01:24:17,558
to engage me in conversation

801
01:24:17,600 --> 01:24:18,601
for your own sake?

802
01:24:18,642 --> 01:24:22,062
I asked you to tell me about your husband.

803
01:24:25,858 --> 01:24:28,027
It's like we're strangers now.

804
01:24:28,694 --> 01:24:29,987
And?

805
01:24:32,156 --> 01:24:34,867
Last time I saw him,
we were so disconnected.

806
01:24:35,451 --> 01:24:37,369
<i>But now...</i>

807
01:24:40,164 --> 01:24:41,373
I'd give...

808
01:24:41,415 --> 01:24:43,417
anything in the world...

809
01:24:46,629 --> 01:24:48,672
to see my husband.

810
01:24:49,673 --> 01:24:51,509
Matrimony has always fascinated me.

811
01:24:51,592 --> 01:24:53,844
Husbands barely
able to look at their wives,

812
01:24:53,886 --> 01:24:58,641
wives on their backs in motel rooms
with perfect strangers,

813
01:24:58,641 --> 01:25:01,560
able to bear
children only to neglect them.

814
01:25:01,602 --> 01:25:03,979
Till death do us part indeed.

815
01:25:04,021 --> 01:25:07,733
I don't know what you think you know,

816
01:25:07,817 --> 01:25:10,736
but my marriage has
survived more suffering

817
01:25:10,820 --> 01:25:13,447
than someone like you could ever grasp.

818
01:25:13,697 --> 01:25:14,573
Suffering?

819
01:25:15,991 --> 01:25:17,743
You haven't seen anything yet.

820
01:25:20,204 --> 01:25:22,665
Someone like me. Who am I?

821
01:25:22,832 --> 01:25:24,500
A monster.

822
01:25:25,209 --> 01:25:27,670
-A murderer.
-I don't condone murder,

823
01:25:27,711 --> 01:25:29,463
and I...

824
01:25:29,964 --> 01:25:31,590
despise murderers.

825
01:25:31,924 --> 01:25:33,425
Please.

826
01:25:39,473 --> 01:25:42,268
Please let me go.

827
01:25:48,649 --> 01:25:51,861
We're fine, Amanda. We don't need you.

828
01:25:56,115 --> 01:25:57,741
I said we're fine.

829
01:26:10,462 --> 01:26:13,549
If you make it through this, Lynn,
you're going to thank me one day--

830
01:26:13,591 --> 01:26:15,259
<i>just as Amanda did.</i>

831
01:26:22,600 --> 01:26:25,728
<i>Please, let me go.</i>

832
01:26:26,604 --> 01:26:28,856
I saved your life.

833
01:26:28,898 --> 01:26:32,318
Maybe my life isn't the one
you were saving after all.

834
01:26:36,322 --> 01:26:40,826
<i>Tell me about your daughter.</i>
<i>I understand she's quite a little athlete.</i>

835
01:26:47,082 --> 01:26:50,502
<i>Or we could talk about your son.</i>

836
01:26:50,544 --> 01:26:51,670
What did you say?

837
01:26:55,090 --> 01:26:59,261
Why are you living with the dead
when you have such a beautiful family?

838
01:26:59,303 --> 01:27:03,432
<i>The husband who's endured alone...</i>

839
01:27:03,474 --> 01:27:06,477
<i>the daughter who needs a mother...</i>

840
01:27:06,518 --> 01:27:09,313
<i>patients who need a competent physician</i>

841
01:27:09,355 --> 01:27:11,315
<i>who looks them in the eye</i>

842
01:27:11,649 --> 01:27:13,442
and treats them like human beings.

843
01:27:13,734 --> 01:27:15,486
He's completed the third test.

844
01:27:17,404 --> 01:27:19,698
Congratulations, Lynn.
You're free to go.

845
01:27:21,367 --> 01:27:23,577
Yeah, but he's not all the way out yet.

846
01:27:25,871 --> 01:27:28,123
Undo her collar, Amanda,
and let her go.

847
01:27:29,375 --> 01:27:32,211
No, he's not finished.
He's not all the way.

848
01:27:32,252 --> 01:27:36,674
Amanda, Lynn is more important
than you know.

849
01:27:37,675 --> 01:27:40,135
Unlock her collar
and let her go.

850
01:27:41,303 --> 01:27:42,471
I said no.

851
01:27:47,184 --> 01:27:48,811
Amanda, there are rules.

852
01:27:48,894 --> 01:27:50,187
I said no!

853
01:27:52,231 --> 01:27:54,024
She doesn't deserve to go free.

854
01:27:54,066 --> 01:27:55,192
You promised.

855
01:27:55,275 --> 01:27:56,819
I didn't promise you shit.

856
01:27:56,860 --> 01:27:59,321
Amanda, even with that gun,

857
01:27:59,363 --> 01:28:00,781
it is Lynn

858
01:28:00,823 --> 01:28:02,700
who holds your life

859
01:28:02,741 --> 01:28:04,451
<i>in her hand.</i>

860
01:28:04,493 --> 01:28:05,285
Fuck you.

861
01:28:05,953 --> 01:28:07,746
You gave her control over me?!

862
01:28:08,163 --> 01:28:09,248
Fuck you!

863
01:28:09,331 --> 01:28:11,583
I won't tell anyone! I promise I won't!

864
01:28:11,667 --> 01:28:13,460
Please, I have a family!

865
01:28:13,544 --> 01:28:15,796
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up!

866
01:28:15,879 --> 01:28:17,965
And stop fuckin' moving around!

867
01:28:18,048 --> 01:28:21,093
And what
about the other test subjects?

868
01:28:22,386 --> 01:28:23,303
What about 'em?

869
01:28:23,345 --> 01:28:25,848
Is that how you thought about them?

870
01:28:27,975 --> 01:28:30,185
Is that how you felt about Eric Matthews?

871
01:28:30,227 --> 01:28:31,603
Game over.

872
01:28:31,687 --> 01:28:33,105
I'll fuckin' kill you!

873
01:28:36,150 --> 01:28:37,234
Eric Matthews?!

874
01:28:38,652 --> 01:28:42,906
I'll tell you how
I felt about Eric Matthews.

875
01:28:54,084 --> 01:28:55,044
Aagh!

876
01:28:55,836 --> 01:28:57,087
<i>Eric Matthews...</i>

877
01:28:57,129 --> 01:29:00,382
learned nothing from your test.

878
01:29:02,676 --> 01:29:05,387
He was the same person he was

879
01:29:05,471 --> 01:29:08,098
when he arrested me...

880
01:29:08,182 --> 01:29:09,767
<i>Daniel!</i>

881
01:29:09,933 --> 01:29:13,062
...when he framed me...

882
01:29:14,605 --> 01:29:16,565
...when he took me down.

883
01:29:59,191 --> 01:30:00,818
Where's my son?

884
01:30:02,903 --> 01:30:05,114
Where is he, you junkie bitch?!

885
01:30:05,155 --> 01:30:06,365
Fuck you.

886
01:30:07,950 --> 01:30:09,660
Where is he?!

887
01:30:21,964 --> 01:30:23,340
<i>Tell me where--</i>

888
01:30:23,841 --> 01:30:25,217
tell me where he is.

889
01:30:25,259 --> 01:30:27,219
Right fuckin' here.

890
01:30:46,572 --> 01:30:48,031
Bitch!

891
01:30:52,995 --> 01:30:54,830
You're nothing, bitch!

892
01:30:56,874 --> 01:30:59,835
<i>You're nothing!</i>

893
01:31:04,047 --> 01:31:06,133
You're not Jigsaw.

894
01:31:10,512 --> 01:31:13,223
You're not Jigsaw, bitch!

895
01:31:22,482 --> 01:31:23,734
You hear me?!

896
01:31:25,277 --> 01:31:26,945
<i>You're nothing!</i>

897
01:31:29,573 --> 01:31:31,783
You're not Jigsaw, bitch.

898
01:31:35,078 --> 01:31:36,663
You're nothing!

899
01:31:40,626 --> 01:31:42,794
<i>I'll fuckin' kill you!</i>

900
01:31:43,045 --> 01:31:44,004
<i>No!</i>

901
01:31:44,046 --> 01:31:45,714
That's right.

902
01:31:45,756 --> 01:31:48,217
I'm a murderer.

903
01:31:48,258 --> 01:31:49,968
He took my life from me.

904
01:31:51,011 --> 01:31:53,055
So I just returned the fuckin' favor.

905
01:31:53,305 --> 01:31:55,432
<i>No, Amanda.</i>
<i>That's what you thought.</i>

906
01:31:55,891 --> 01:31:57,476
But I know different.

907
01:31:59,061 --> 01:32:02,481
<i>-You left him for dead, didn't you?</i>
-Stop fucking with me.

908
01:32:03,232 --> 01:32:05,817
<i>But I cleaned up your mistakes.</i>

909
01:32:06,193 --> 01:32:08,528
And I forgave you for them.

910
01:32:12,532 --> 01:32:15,244
<i>What you do</i>
<i>is no different than murder.</i>

911
01:32:15,285 --> 01:32:16,954
<i>You torture people.</i>

912
01:32:16,995 --> 01:32:18,497
You watch them die.

913
01:32:18,580 --> 01:32:21,792
But now you're begging me
not to kill this worthless bitch

914
01:32:21,875 --> 01:32:23,335
on the grounds of some game?

915
01:32:23,418 --> 01:32:26,463
You're walking us
towards a precipice, Amanda.

916
01:32:26,630 --> 01:32:28,799
-<i>Step back.</i>
-It's bullshit.

917
01:32:28,966 --> 01:32:30,259
<i>Nobody changes.</i>

918
01:32:31,301 --> 01:32:32,177
<i>It's all a lie.</i>

919
01:32:32,594 --> 01:32:36,682
If you fail in this, we all fail.
Succeed, and we all succeed.

920
01:32:36,723 --> 01:32:38,016
It's a lie!

921
01:32:44,022 --> 01:32:46,275
I'll tell
you she hasn't changed...

922
01:32:46,900 --> 01:32:49,319
because nobody fuckin' changes.

923
01:32:50,737 --> 01:32:53,824
Nobody is reborn.
It's all bullshit!

924
01:32:54,283 --> 01:32:58,662
It's all a fuckin' lie!
And I'm just a pawn in your stupid games.

925
01:33:11,717 --> 01:33:14,052
I don't mean anything to you.

926
01:33:14,219 --> 01:33:16,722
No, you mean everything to me.

927
01:33:16,763 --> 01:33:18,348
<i>Fuck you!</i>

928
01:33:18,390 --> 01:33:20,434
Our fates are linked.

929
01:33:21,560 --> 01:33:23,979
I've tried to help you, Amanda.

930
01:33:24,021 --> 01:33:25,939
So, help me!

931
01:33:26,064 --> 01:33:27,607
<i>Fix me.</i>

932
01:33:29,151 --> 01:33:30,777
Fix me, motherfucker!

933
01:33:32,070 --> 01:33:34,031
I'm standing right here.

934
01:33:38,493 --> 01:33:41,496
Why is she so important to you?

935
01:33:42,331 --> 01:33:44,374
She's not important to me.

936
01:33:46,168 --> 01:33:47,919
She's important to you.

937
01:33:47,961 --> 01:33:50,130
She's not important to me.

938
01:33:50,172 --> 01:33:51,757
I beg you...

939
01:33:52,257 --> 01:33:53,842
to reconsider that.

940
01:33:58,972 --> 01:34:01,266
This is your last chance, Amanda.

941
01:34:01,308 --> 01:34:02,851
She's nothing.

942
01:34:19,659 --> 01:34:21,787
Your time is running out.

943
01:34:24,956 --> 01:34:27,084
Now you think about what you are doing.

944
01:34:30,045 --> 01:34:33,715
<i>Think about</i>
<i>everything that you've done.</i>

945
01:34:40,222 --> 01:34:43,308
You think
about what you promised me.

946
01:34:43,725 --> 01:34:45,227
<i>Think about our dreams.</i>

947
01:34:46,478 --> 01:34:48,063
Think about tomorrow.

948
01:34:51,149 --> 01:34:51,900
Lynn?

949
01:34:52,692 --> 01:34:54,403
<i>-Jeff?!</i>
<i>-No!</i>

950
01:34:55,862 --> 01:34:56,863
Lynn!

951
01:35:01,284 --> 01:35:02,369
Jeff.

952
01:35:03,495 --> 01:35:05,163
You just destroyed 4 lives.

953
01:35:06,540 --> 01:35:08,125
You just murdered Jeff's wife.

954
01:35:30,063 --> 01:35:31,189
Amanda...

955
01:35:33,733 --> 01:35:34,943
It's ok.

956
01:35:40,657 --> 01:35:42,284
This was your destiny.

957
01:35:44,453 --> 01:35:45,412
Your game.

958
01:35:47,289 --> 01:35:48,665
What do I want?

959
01:35:48,999 --> 01:35:50,667
I want to play a game.

960
01:35:53,086 --> 01:35:55,297
You are being tested.
Your will is being tested--

961
01:35:55,338 --> 01:35:58,758
your will to keep someone alive.
Can you do that?

962
01:35:58,842 --> 01:36:02,596
Can you follow the rules
and grant someone the gift of life?

963
01:36:04,848 --> 01:36:06,641
I was testing you.

964
01:36:06,892 --> 01:36:08,226
<i>I took you in.</i>

965
01:36:08,268 --> 01:36:10,687
You will give everything to me.

966
01:36:10,729 --> 01:36:11,730
Yes.

967
01:36:11,771 --> 01:36:13,064
Every cell in your body.

968
01:36:13,106 --> 01:36:14,191
<i>I selected you...</i>

969
01:36:14,232 --> 01:36:18,737
<i>for the honor of</i>
<i>carrying on my life's work.</i>

970
01:36:19,321 --> 01:36:20,947
<i>-But you didn't.</i>
-That's right.

971
01:36:23,033 --> 01:36:24,075
I'm a murderer.

972
01:36:24,117 --> 01:36:25,452
I despise murderers.

973
01:36:25,535 --> 01:36:27,871
<i>You didn't test anyone's will to live.</i>

974
01:36:27,913 --> 01:36:29,331
Game over.

975
01:36:30,624 --> 01:36:32,876
<i> Instead,</i>
<i>you took away their only chance.</i>

976
01:36:32,918 --> 01:36:34,961
<i>Your games were unwinnable.</i>

977
01:36:35,962 --> 01:36:38,006
<i>Your subjects merely victims.</i>

978
01:36:38,048 --> 01:36:39,007
You.

979
01:36:40,300 --> 01:36:43,345
There is no turning back.
Do you understand that?

980
01:36:43,637 --> 01:36:44,679
<i>In my desperation,</i>

981
01:36:44,721 --> 01:36:48,225
<i>I decided to give you one last chance.</i>

982
01:36:49,059 --> 01:36:52,437
<i>So, I put everything in place.</i>

983
01:36:52,479 --> 01:36:54,648
You chose
her 'cause she's the best, right?

984
01:36:54,689 --> 01:36:56,441
That's one reason I chose her.

985
01:36:56,483 --> 01:37:00,820
<i>You didn't know that Lynn and Jeff</i>
<i>were husband and wife.</i>

986
01:37:01,279 --> 01:37:05,492
<i>I had to keep that from you</i>
<i>for the purposes of my game.</i>

987
01:37:05,534 --> 01:37:08,578
<i>I had to leave out the ruined marriage</i>

988
01:37:08,620 --> 01:37:11,373
<i>the cheating wife...</i>

989
01:37:11,414 --> 01:37:16,711
<i>the vengeful husband,</i>
<i>the neglected daughter.</i>

990
01:37:16,753 --> 01:37:18,463
<i>And I let you...</i>

991
01:37:18,505 --> 01:37:20,507
<i>make your own choices.</i>

992
01:37:21,758 --> 01:37:24,719
I wanted you to succeed.

993
01:37:25,887 --> 01:37:26,888
<i>Amanda!</i>

994
01:37:26,930 --> 01:37:28,265
Put it away.

995
01:37:28,306 --> 01:37:29,391
Trust me.

996
01:37:29,391 --> 01:37:30,475
Even with that gun,

997
01:37:30,517 --> 01:37:34,271
it is Lynn who holds
your life in her hands.

998
01:37:34,312 --> 01:37:35,647
She's not important to me.

999
01:37:36,273 --> 01:37:38,483
I beg you to reconsider that.

1000
01:37:38,525 --> 01:37:41,027
Unlock her collar and let her go.

1001
01:37:41,069 --> 01:37:42,279
I said no!

1002
01:37:43,238 --> 01:37:45,240
The rules of our game
have been made very clear.

1003
01:37:45,282 --> 01:37:48,326
You need to abide by those rules.

1004
01:37:49,744 --> 01:37:50,954
You couldn't.

1005
01:37:57,419 --> 01:37:58,920
God.

1006
01:38:14,894 --> 01:38:16,646
Game over.

1007
01:38:27,616 --> 01:38:30,452
<i>You haven't</i>
<i>learned anything tonight, have you?</i>

1008
01:38:30,452 --> 01:38:34,664
Your rage and your vengeance
will only hurt the ones you love.

1009
01:38:35,206 --> 01:38:40,629
Killing me will only add to your misery.
It will not bring back your son.

1010
01:38:40,670 --> 01:38:42,547
Think of your daughter, Jeff.

1011
01:38:42,589 --> 01:38:46,468
She needs you now more than ever.

1012
01:38:46,885 --> 01:38:49,304
You can't kill me, Jeff.

1013
01:38:59,272 --> 01:39:01,066
Your wife's dying, Jeff.

1014
01:39:02,317 --> 01:39:04,361
<i>Her time's running out.</i>

1015
01:39:12,619 --> 01:39:13,578
Jeff?

1016
01:39:13,620 --> 01:39:15,705
Do not miscalculate.

1017
01:39:15,997 --> 01:39:21,211
<i>Your fate is in my hands.</i>
<i>Your wife's fate is in my hands.</i>

1018
01:39:21,252 --> 01:39:23,463
<i> I love you.</i>

1019
01:39:23,505 --> 01:39:25,632
I love you.

1020
01:39:28,468 --> 01:39:31,054
I'm taking you home, ok?

1021
01:39:31,096 --> 01:39:33,682
Though you may not see any threat...

1022
01:39:34,474 --> 01:39:37,102
there are threats all around you.

1023
01:39:37,143 --> 01:39:39,437
Jeff, if you try to move your wife,

1024
01:39:39,479 --> 01:39:40,522
<i>she will die.</i>

1025
01:39:40,522 --> 01:39:42,899
<i>I can have an ambulance here in 4 minutes.</i>

1026
01:39:43,483 --> 01:39:45,527
Would you like to take
your wife out of here tonight?

1027
01:39:45,568 --> 01:39:48,029
Would you like to take her to safety?

1028
01:39:48,071 --> 01:39:48,863
Stay.

1029
01:39:48,905 --> 01:39:50,490
<i>Stand and face me, Jeff.</i>

1030
01:39:50,532 --> 01:39:51,533
Stay with me.

1031
01:39:51,574 --> 01:39:52,534
<i>Right now.</i>

1032
01:39:52,575 --> 01:39:53,660
Please...

1033
01:39:53,702 --> 01:39:56,162
<i>Would you like to get your life back?</i>

1034
01:39:57,455 --> 01:40:00,834
<i>Would you, Jeff?</i>
<i>I can make that happen.</i>

1035
01:40:02,502 --> 01:40:04,087
Which is it, Jeff?

1036
01:40:04,129 --> 01:40:05,964
<i>Come on.</i>

1037
01:40:06,005 --> 01:40:06,965
<i>Yes or no?</i>

1038
01:40:07,090 --> 01:40:07,966
Yes.

1039
01:40:10,844 --> 01:40:12,512
What do you want?

1040
01:40:12,554 --> 01:40:15,557
One final test.
The rules are simple.

1041
01:40:15,557 --> 01:40:16,891
Over on that table...

1042
01:40:16,933 --> 01:40:20,979
there's a host of vicious implements...

